<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <.chrome here="Terms"></.chrome>

  <div class="pbody legal-doc">
    <.section title="About these terms" pad>
      <p>
        cab is a free service of the NGO Debate Federation of Ukraine (ВМГО «Федерація Дебатів
        України») for running debate clubs and their sessions. By using it you agree to these
        terms. How we handle personal data is in the <.link href={~p"/policy"}>Policy</.link>.
      </p>
      <p class="mut">Last updated: 9 October 2026.</p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Accounts and personal links" pad>
      <p>
        Sign in with your own account and keep it to yourself. A personal guest link is your
        access to one session: anyone holding it acts as you, so share it with no one.
        You can move a guest's results into your own account once you sign in.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Club heads" pad>
      <p>
        A club head runs the club page, decides on join requests and runs the sessions: who
        registers, who sits where, motions and ballots. A club head adds people only with their
        agreement and treats what members write in their requests as confidential.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Fair use" pad>
      <p>
        Use cab for debating. Do not impersonate others, enter false results, harass anyone
        in names, motions or messages, or try to break, overload or get around the service's
        access rules. We may remove content or suspend access that breaks these terms, and we
        say why when we do.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Results" pad>
      <p>
        Ballots and results are the record of a debate. Once a session is finished they stay,
        including in standings, so that the club's history is complete. Mistakes are
        corrected by the club head.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Beta" pad>
      <p>
        cab is in beta testing. It is offered as it is, may change, and may be unavailable at
        times. We keep the data safe and backed up, but we cannot promise the service is free
        of errors. To the extent the law allows, the Federation is not liable for indirect
        losses from using cab.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Changes and law" pad>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; we change the date above and say so on this page before a
        change applies. These terms are governed by the law of Ukraine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:ngo.dfu@uadebate.com">ngo.dfu@uadebate.com</a>. Support: <a href="mailto:support@uadebate.com">support@uadebate.com</a>.
      </p>
    </.section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
